<title>USA: Stepan buying surfacant business.</title>
<headline>Stepan buying surfacant business.</headline>
<dateline>NORTHFIELD, Ill. 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stepan Co said Friday it signed a definitive agreement to acquire the West Coast anionic and selected surfactant business used in shampoos from Lonza Inc for undisclosed terms.</p>
<p>Lonza's West Coast operation is in Long Beach, Calif. No manufacturing facilities were included in the transaction, which is expected to close on April 1.</p>
<p>Stepan produces specialty and intermediate chemicals used in household, industrial, personal care, agricultural and food products.</p>
<p>	  ((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
